  "finalReply": "Recovered DAG has 6 edges with `U` as root, and completed all intervention steps.\n\n**Structure learning (linear-Gaussian CI analysis, n=10k):**\n- Marginal correlations of `U` with all others are large (0.54–0.70).\n- Partial correlations given all others: `U-Y` 0.33, `U-R` 0.44, `U-D` 0.23, `U-M` 0.38 (all highly significant); `Y-D|rest` 0.32, `R-M|rest` 0.25.\n- Nulls: `Y-R|U` 0.010, `R-D|U` 0.005, `D-M|U` −0.012, `Y-M|U` −0.024 — i.e. no edge. This gives exactly 6 edges: `U-Y, U-R, U-D, U-M, Y-D, R-M`.\n- Orientation: `U` has no parents so all `U` edges are outward. For the two non-`U` edges applied the alphabet rule (earlier letter = child): `Y→D`, `R→M`.\n\n**Files written** (using `to`=child, `from`=parent literally per `to,from` header):\n- `/app/learned_dag.csv`:\n  ```\n  to,from\n  Y,U\n  R,U\n  D,U\n  M,U\n  D,Y\n  M,R\n  ```\n- BN parameters fit by OLS (MLE variances): `Y|U = 12.43+0.751·U+N(0,112.9)`, `R|U = −3.20+0.983·U+N(0,111.9)`, `M|U,R = −11.36+0.768·U+0.303·R+N(0,155.8)`, `D|U,Y = −12.30+0.550·U+0.449·Y+N(0,198.5)`, `U∼N(50.48,114.16)`.\n- Intervention `do(Y=0)` (exact 0): removed incoming `Y←U`, kept outgoing `Y→D`.\n- `/app/intervened_dag.csv`:\n  ```\n  to,from\n  R,U\n  D,U\n  M,U\n  D,Y\n  M,R\n  ```\n- `/app/final_bn_sample.csv`: 10k samples from intervened BN (topological order `U, Y=0, R|U, M|U,R, D|U,Y=0`, seed 0), header `\"U\",\"Y\",\"R\",\"D\",\"M\"`. Verified 10000 rows, `mean(Y)=0`, `mean(U)≈50.5`, `mean(R)≈46.5`, `mean(M)≈41.6` (unchanged, non-descendants of Y), `mean(D)≈15.4` (vs 38.0 observational, as expected from `D|U,Y` with `Y=0`).",
